{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>הוי</b> — Some say: like אוי, or הוי is a word of calling, like הוי ציון המלטי." "<b>כלה</b> — In every passage, 'a place of ways, streets thereof' is filled with כחש, and the word ימיש is a verb in pausal form [יוצא רגל, lit. 'foot-exiting', i.e. pausal/absolute], and it means 'she is so filled with כחש to deceive the world'; each one of them does not withdraw himself from the prey."], :book :nahum, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {1 "The phrase בכל פרק appears to quote Nahum 3:1 fragmentarily; translated hyper-literally as it stands. ימיש פועל יוצא likely means ימיש is a verb in absolute/pausal form (יוצא = not in construct chain); rendered literally. The repeated כחש (deceit/falsehood) is preserved."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Nahum -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/nachum"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:14:40.526009099Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}